```console
$ sonicmux --help
Make MKV audio playable on TVs without re-encoding video.

Usage: sonicmux [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  probe        Inspect streams, chapters, attachments, and metadata
  convert      Convert incompatible audio or remux existing compatible audio
  scan         Find MKV files and show the actions they require
  config       Inspect and manage configuration
  presets      List and inspect device presets
  doctor       Check FFmpeg and required codec capabilities
  completions  Generate shell completion scripts
  man          Generate a manual page
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --config <PATH>
          Use this TOML configuration file

      --ffmpeg-path <PATH>
          Use this FFmpeg executable or installation directory

      --json
          Write the final result as JSON to stdout

      --json-progress
          Write versioned NDJSON events to stdout

      --color <COLOR>
          Color output

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Detect terminal support and `NO_COLOR`
          - always: Always emit terminal color
          - never:  Never emit terminal color

      --log-file <PATH>
          Also write structured diagnostic logs to a file

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase diagnostic verbosity

  -q, --quiet
          Hide non-error human output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

```

```console
$ sonicmux probe --help
Inspect streams, chapters, attachments, and metadata

Usage: sonicmux probe [OPTIONS] <INPUT>...

Arguments:
  <INPUT>...
          MKV files to inspect

Options:
      --compact
          Show one summary row per file

      --config <PATH>
          Use this TOML configuration file

      --ffmpeg-path <PATH>
          Use this FFmpeg executable or installation directory

      --json
          Write the final result as JSON to stdout

      --json-progress
          Write versioned NDJSON events to stdout

      --color <COLOR>
          Color output

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Detect terminal support and `NO_COLOR`
          - always: Always emit terminal color
          - never:  Never emit terminal color

      --log-file <PATH>
          Also write structured diagnostic logs to a file

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase diagnostic verbosity

  -q, --quiet
          Hide non-error human output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

```

```console
$ sonicmux convert --help
Convert incompatible audio or remux existing compatible audio

Usage: sonicmux convert [OPTIONS] <INPUT>...

Arguments:
  <INPUT>...
          MKV files, directories, or glob patterns

Options:
      --config <PATH>
          Use this TOML configuration file

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Device profile

      --codec <CODEC>
          Target audio codec
[..]
          [possible values: ac3, eac3, aac]

      --ffmpeg-path <PATH>
          Use this FFmpeg executable or installation directory

      --bitrate <RATE>
          Target bitrate, for example 640k

      --json
          Write the final result as JSON to stdout

      --channels <CHANNELS>
          Output layout
[..]
          [possible values: keep-up-to-5.1, stereo, 5.1]

      --json-progress
          Write versioned NDJSON events to stdout

      --color <COLOR>
          Color output

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Detect terminal support and `NO_COLOR`
          - always: Always emit terminal color
          - never:  Never emit terminal color

      --mode <MODE>
          Audio output mode
[..]
          [possible values: add, replace, only-new]

      --log-file <PATH>
          Also write structured diagnostic logs to a file

  -r, --recursive
          Recurse into input directories

      --include <GLOB>
          Include matching relative paths

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase diagnostic verbosity

      --exclude <GLOB>
          Exclude matching relative paths

  -q, --quiet
          Hide non-error human output

      --follow-links
          Follow symbolic links

      --remux-only
          Remux an existing compatible audio track without encoding

      --default-audio <DEFAULT_AUDIO>
          Track for remux: index, language, or first-compatible
[..]
          [default: first-compatible]

  -o, --output <PATH>
          Exact output path; requires one discovered input

      --output-dir <DIR>
          Put generated outputs in this existing directory

      --dry-run
          Probe and print plans without writing files

      --jobs <N>
          Maximum files processed at once

      --storage-profile <STORAGE_PROFILE>
          Storage concurrency profile

          Possible values:
          - hdd:      Rotational or seek-sensitive storage; defaults to one job
          - balanced: Conservative general-purpose concurrency
          - nvme:     Explicit solid-state storage intent

      --continue-on-error
          Continue the batch after a file fails (default)

      --fail-fast
          Stop admission and cancel active files after the first failure

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

```

